Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.78,0:00:08.49,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.49,0:00:11.16,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.16,0:00:15.83,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.95,0:01:36.66,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,What?! Eren Senpai's missing?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.78,0:01:40.67,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,I only turned my back for one second...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.67,0:01:44.79,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,It's hard to believe that easily scared \NEren Senpai would go off on her own.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.79,0:01:46.58,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Well, it makes sense if she was scared.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.98,0:01:49.46,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,It's dangerous here, ya know?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.46,0:01:53.60,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Maybe she noticed the tension \Nin the air and ran off.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.13,0:01:58.43,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,You're making sense for a change. \NNot bad for a deadhead.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.43,0:01:59.89,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Don't say that!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.45,0:02:03.73,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,I know that better than anyone else...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.21,0:02:05.69,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Sorry to interrupt.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.03,0:02:08.99,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Allow me to introduce \Nthe newest member of our group.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.99,0:02:12.15,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,I'm Rika Suzuki. Nice to meet y'all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.15,0:02:12.90,Default,Jin,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.90,0:02:18.04,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Ay, Omi Jin, was it? \NSorry 'bout the other day.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.04,0:02:20.72,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,You gave me a huge wake-up call, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.72,0:02:21.54,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.54,0:02:26.83,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,What you said to me that day, \Ntowards someone who tried to kill you...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.15,0:02:30.30,Flashback,Omi,0,0,0,,See ya! Hope you stay alive, Suzuki-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.80,0:02:36.76,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Thanks, Omi Jin. I owe you for making \NRika Suzuki become human again.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.05,0:02:39.60,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,N-Nah. I didn't do nothin'...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.13,0:02:41.22,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Your leg...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.22,0:02:43.72,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Oh, it was in exchange for my Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.72,0:02:48.01,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,She possesses the Evasion Right, \Nwhich nullifies any kind of physical harm.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.01,0:02:51.25,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Stand next to her and you'll \Nalso be protected by extension.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.70,0:02:53.07,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Great.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.07,0:02:57.20,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,From now on, let's station Rika \Nand Omi in our location for the day.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.20,0:03:00.28,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,We can use the Rejection Right \Nand Evasion Right to protect us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.28,0:03:04.08,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Right. Now back to Eren Senpai...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.08,0:03:06.15,Default-Top,Gobo,0,0,0,,You think she'll come back on her own?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.43,0:03:07.38,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Well, that was easy. No rebuttals?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.15,0:03:07.38,Default-Top,Saaya,0,0,0,,Should we wait until tomorrow, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.38,0:03:08.93,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,They trust him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.93,0:03:09.71,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.01,0:03:13.73,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Saneatsu Narita... Not an owner of a \NPrime Right or any significant titles.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.73,0:03:16.38,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,And yet, his peers all respect and trust him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.86,0:03:18.22,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Interesting, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.60,0:03:19.88,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Huh...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.58,0:03:23.18,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Saneatsu...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.18,0:03:24.85,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,What's up, Saaya?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.10,0:03:25.23,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\fs15\frz308\pos(175,329)}Prime\NRight
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.20,0:03:26.19,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,I found this.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.23,0:03:26.19,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\fs15\pos(292,234)\frz339.2}Prime\NRight
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.19,0:03:27.97,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,A Prime Right envelope?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.97,0:03:29.55,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,It was in this building.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.55,0:03:31.37,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,I thought about opening it,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.37,0:03:34.15,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,but I couldn't stop thinking of \Nwhat I'd have to sacrifice, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.15,0:03:35.53,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\fs15\pos(292,234)\frz339.2}Prime\NRight
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.15,0:03:37.36,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,No need to apologize. \NThat's totally reasonable.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.53,0:03:35.65,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\fs15\pos(292,234)\frz339.2\clip(m 266 236 l 271 264 316 283 331 248 266 217)}Prime\NRight
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.65,0:03:36.90,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\fs15\pos(292,234)\frz339.2\clip(m 274 256 l 276 267 316 283 331 248 269 217)}Prime\NRight
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.90,0:03:40.70,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,If I just open it myself...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.70,0:03:42.66,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Saneatsu?! What are you—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.66,0:03:45.88,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I promised I'd defeat \Nthe Emperor... that I'd fight!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.88,0:03:48.23,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,W-Wait! Let's think about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.96,0:03:51.76,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,What're you two love birds talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.76,0:03:53.67,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Hey! Don't tell me that's...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.67,0:03:55.26,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\fax-0.2\fs30\frz146.3\pos(387,127)}Prime\NRight
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.67,0:03:55.26,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Is that a Prime Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.26,0:03:59.04,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Perfect timing! Kazuhiko, \Nyou're on defense. Block Saaya!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.04,0:04:00.26,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,M'kay!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.97,0:04:04.18,Default-Top,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Defense! Defense! Defense!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.79,0:04:04.18,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Umm...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.18,0:04:08.88,Default-Top,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Defense! Defense! Defense!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.18,0:04:08.88,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Saaya, don't worry. This is what I want.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.23,0:04:13.98,Italics,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I'm such a fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.98,0:04:17.97,Italics,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,How could I forget why I became \Na teacher in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.82,0:04:20.50,Italics,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I won't lose my way again!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.70,0:04:23.37,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,This must be it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.24,0:04:28.83,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Huh?! What's this note?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.83,0:04:30.37,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Here goes nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.76,0:04:34.21,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,What? Even if that's true, how could...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.25,0:04:37.69,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I have to tell him before it's too late!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.59,0:04:39.47,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,1)\bord0\fs13\shad0\frz17\an8\pos(273,100)\frx10\fry16}Prime Right Access Denied\N You are not permitted to\N acquire a Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.47,0:04:40.30,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.30,0:04:43.76,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\shad0\pos(313,347)}Prime Right Access Denied
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.05,0:04:43.76,Default-Top,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I can't acquire a Prime Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.22,0:04:46.93,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I have to hurry and tell Narita!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.52,0:04:50.19,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,An error when acquiring Prime Rights?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.19,0:04:52.35,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Do you have any idea what might cause it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.35,0:04:54.32,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Hmm... Beats me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.32,0:04:56.56,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Maybe only if you already \Nhave a Prime Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.56,0:04:59.71,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,or you happen to fall into another \Nspecial rule that blocks you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.71,0:05:03.82,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Those are the only \Npossibilities I can think of.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.82,0:05:05.05,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Omi-kun, if you don't mind,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.05,0:05:09.41,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,could you tell us everything you know \Nabout the Camp and Prime Rights?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.41,0:05:10.79,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.54,0:05:17.99,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,The Camp is at the border \Nbetween Tokyo and Chiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.99,0:05:20.39,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,It's a giant facility built \N100 meters underground.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.88,0:05:22.39,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,100 meters?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.39,0:05:24.76,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,A giant facility hidden \Nbeneath the metro area...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.14,0:05:30.68,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,The facility was designed so that no one \Nwould find it. There were ten areas.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.68,0:05:32.67,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I was at Area A.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.67,0:05:36.86,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I never saw Sensei and that macho guy, \Nso they must be from another area.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.27,0:05:39.74,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Why were you there in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.16,0:05:44.41,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I'm originally from the Tohoku Region... \Na small town in Aomori.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.99,0:05:48.87,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Five years ago, some men \Ncame to visit our home.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.39,0:05:52.46,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Apparently, they'd been\N introduced to my dad's company.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.85,0:05:54.93,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,They were there to recruit my dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.54,0:06:01.17,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,He gladly agreed and we all left together \Nas a family, in hopes of a better future.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.76,0:06:04.94,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,My memory gets fuzzy after that, \Nand before I knew it...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.31,0:06:12.27,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Wha—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.52,0:06:16.52,Flashback,Omi,0,0,0,,Dad? Mom? Where are ya?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.52,0:06:17.57,Flashback,Man,0,0,0,,Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.45,0:06:24.15,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,The Camp targeted isolated households \Nin rural areas with little to no relatives
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.15,0:06:27.87,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,so it would be harder to track, \Nand used them in their experiments.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.49,0:06:30.37,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,They tricked my entire family.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.30,0:06:35.04,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I was forced into the lab every month \Nwithout ever seeing them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.47,0:06:38.46,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,They threatened to kill \Nmy family if I didn't listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.46,0:06:40.67,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,And that lasted three years...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.00,0:06:44.56,Flashback,Researcher 1,0,0,0,,Let's see... What if we sacrificed...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.56,0:06:45.97,Flashback,Researcher 1,0,0,0,,Your right eye, perhaps?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.15,0:06:51.52,Flashback,Researcher 1,0,0,0,,If you resist, I'll just \Nmake it more "efficient".
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.50,0:06:56.60,Flashback,Researcher 1,0,0,0,,Damn it, I missed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.60,0:06:58.72,Flashback,Researcher 2 (Mido),0,0,0,,Aww, that's too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.11,0:07:04.65,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,The stab went so deep that \NI lost hearing in my right ear.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.65,0:07:07.21,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,You mean that band aid is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.21,0:07:09.40,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,It's how I hide the scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.40,0:07:12.48,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,After that, I was so desperate \Nto relieve the pain and fear
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.48,0:07:14.37,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,that I accessed my Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.65,0:07:20.91,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,They only experimented on the most tractable member of the family.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.91,0:07:23.47,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,To prevent the rest from conspiring...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.47,0:07:24.76,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,they were killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.06,0:07:30.68,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Because of me, both of my parents died...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.86,0:07:33.67,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Omi...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.67,0:07:35.14,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,That's bullshit!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.14,0:07:36.94,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,No way it's your fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.94,0:07:39.22,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,None of it would've happened \Nif it wasn't for them!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.22,0:07:42.23,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Screw those fat, flaming, \Nstinking pieces of garbage!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.23,0:07:45.86,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,And... and... Argh! \NThis really pisses me off!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.86,0:07:47.47,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Hey, pea size!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.47,0:07:48.79,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Don't waste time crying! Get pissed!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.79,0:07:51.37,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,We'll make sure to kick their ass together!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.37,0:07:54.87,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Dammit, I'm still so pissed off!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.44,0:07:56.06,Default-Top,Saaya,0,0,0,,Let's get you cooled down, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.06,0:07:58.16,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Can you believe those guys?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.06,0:07:58.16,Default-Top,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Now, now. Here, vent to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.16,0:07:59.33,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,I get how you feel, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.33,0:08:00.19,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Hey... come on! Let go!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.19,0:08:01.05,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,You take it from here!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.05,0:08:02.59,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,I'm still pissed, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.36,0:08:07.01,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Omi, is there anything else \Nyou can tell us about the Camp?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.29,0:08:11.51,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,It used to have branches \Noverseas, too, but now...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.87,0:08:15.47,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,There was a huge breach \Nat the facility two years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.88,0:08:20.24,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,That was when we all escaped. \NBut most of us were captured.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.66,0:08:24.39,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I reported the facility wherever \NI could, but no one believed me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.39,0:08:25.83,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.83,0:08:27.44,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Here's my theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.88,0:08:30.91,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,The Camp's objective was \Nto find certain Prime Rights,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.91,0:08:34.49,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,and they forced prisoners \Nto acquire powers in search of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.49,0:08:37.25,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,The Emperor must be the success.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.25,0:08:42.71,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,What do you mean? \NAren't there only 65 Prime Rights?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.97,0:08:46.28,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I've seen the Storage Room before.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.28,0:08:49.11,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,These weren't just a couple hundred \Nenvelopes... there were way more.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.11,0:08:52.80,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Jeez. Can you imagine if you had all of them?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.10,0:08:55.48,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,"All of them"? Hang on...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.48,0:08:59.52,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Omi, how many prisoners would \Nyou say there were? A bunch?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.52,0:09:01.60,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Huh? Well, ya...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.60,0:09:04.52,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,What do you think happened \Nto the ones who were captured?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.83,0:09:07.88,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Well, I'd assume they were all killed...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.88,0:09:10.49,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,And what happens to a \NPrime Right if the owner dies?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.77,0:09:15.49,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Omi, would there be any other way \Nto acquire Prime Rights?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.82,0:09:19.10,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Opening the envelope is the only way.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.10,0:09:22.84,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Oh, but I guess you could \Nbe threatened to open it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.84,0:09:25.20,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Or someone else could \Nmake you open one by force,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.20,0:09:27.87,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,if the body part in exchange is visible.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.34,0:09:31.99,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,But you can only own one \NPrime Right per person.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.99,0:09:33.34,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Don't you see?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.91,0:09:36.31,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,The point is to have the general \Npublic open the envelopes,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.31,0:09:39.41,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,then kill them to recover \Nthe abandoned Prime Rights.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.41,0:09:40.93,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Of course, I get it now!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.30,0:09:44.81,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,The Emperor already has a Prime Right, \Nmeaning they can't open other envelopes!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.81,0:09:49.24,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,So they scattered the remaining envelopes \Nfor other people to open!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.24,0:09:53.24,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Exactly. The Emperor's Prime Right \Nis likely the Recovery Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.24,0:09:55.09,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,And their goal is to recover \Nother Prime Rights.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.09,0:09:56.66,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Recovery Right?
Dialogue: 1,0:09:56.66,0:09:59.15,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Prime Rights are limited to one per person,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.66,0:10:06.88,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(322,107)}Prime       Right
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.66,0:10:13.05,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(306,239)}Recovery      Right
Dialogue: 1,0:09:59.15,0:10:01.40,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,but as long as the Emperor \Nis set as the recovery destination,
Dialogue: 1,0:10:01.40,0:10:03.96,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,they can collect as many \NPrime Rights as they want.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.91,0:10:05.50,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,1)\pos(130,91)}Prime
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.91,0:10:05.96,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,1)\pos(522,91)}Prime
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.91,0:10:06.54,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,1)\pos(547,258)}Prime
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.91,0:10:06.92,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,1)\pos(105,258)}Prime
Dialogue: 1,0:10:03.96,0:10:05.93,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Tasuketsu was likely made possible
Dialogue: 1,0:10:05.93,0:10:10.18,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,due to the collected powers \Nof those numerous Prime Rights!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.88,0:10:09.55,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(322,115)}Prime
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.55,0:10:13.05,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(322,95)}Prime
Dialogue: 1,0:10:10.18,0:10:13.05,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,But this is all just a theory \Nbased on the assumption
Dialogue: 1,0:10:13.05,0:10:17.89,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,that people lose ownership \Nof Prime Rights when they die.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.29,0:10:20.47,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Then we'll have to prove that's the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.81,0:10:25.94,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Which is why we'll have to \Nsee him again to be sure...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.94,0:10:27.94,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(492,245)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.46,0:10:27.63,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Ren Iruga.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.90,0:10:31.86,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Maybe I made a mistake,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.86,0:10:35.78,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,but there's no way we can find \None laptop in the whole of Kita Ward.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.69,0:10:39.24,Default,Mob Guy 1,0,0,0,,Hey, look. A girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.20,0:10:41.24,Default,Mob Guy 1,0,0,0,,What are you thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.24,0:10:43.25,Default,Mob Guy 2,0,0,0,,I guess we can have some fun \Nbefore killing her.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.25,0:10:44.08,Default,Mob Guy 1,0,0,0,,I'll go ahead, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.08,0:10:46.67,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,You two, crash into that convenience store!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.67,0:10:48.25,Default,Mob Guy 1,0,0,0,,As you wish!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.25,0:10:49.13,Default,Mob Guy 2,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.88,0:10:51.84,Italics,Eren,0,0,0,,It only worked on one?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.31,0:10:58.82,Default,Mob Guy 2,0,0,0,,You bitch!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.82,0:11:08.12,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,You there, are you hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.85,0:11:13.03,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,There, there. Good job.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.03,0:11:18.88,Italics,Eren,0,0,0,,Isn't this the guy with \Nthe Materialization Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.24,0:11:23.20,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,It's safe here. No need to be afraid.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.57,0:11:25.78,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I don't plan to hurt any normal people.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.56,0:11:27.58,Italics-Top,Eren,0,0,0,,Wait, he doesn't recognize me?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.58,0:11:31.42,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Oh, I'm sorry. Thank you for helping me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.42,0:11:36.26,Default,s,0,0,0,,You swooped in out of nowhere \Nlike a hero. I'm still in shock.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.77,0:11:39.89,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Hero, huh...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.68,0:11:42.08,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.08,0:11:44.48,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,What would you do if...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.62,0:11:49.64,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,if someone you considered \Na hero sold his soul?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.64,0:11:52.00,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Are you talking about a manga or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.00,0:11:55.68,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,'Course not. It's about \Na man who saved my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.16,0:11:59.64,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I'll never forget that day, ten years ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.49,0:12:03.10,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I accidentally caused a fire at my house.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.44,0:12:07.62,Flashback,Younger Souma,0,0,0,,H-Help... me...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.11,0:12:07.62,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,{\an8}Anyone here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.05,0:12:10.46,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Hey! You okay?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.34,0:12:13.45,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.45,0:12:14.58,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Does it hurt anywhere?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.58,0:12:16.16,Flashback,Younger Souma,0,0,0,,I was... cooking and...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.82,0:12:21.53,Flashback,Younger Souma,0,0,0,,It was my fault. I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.41,0:12:19.23,Flashback - Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,You're safe. That's all that matters!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.23,0:12:21.53,Flashback - Top,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Forget about anything else!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.46,0:12:29.23,Flashback,Younger Souma,0,0,0,,I liked to cook, but I'm gonna quit.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.23,0:12:32.96,Flashback,Younger Souma,0,0,0,,This all happened cause \NI wanted to make family happy...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.40,0:12:35.02,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Don't say that!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.34,0:12:36.20,Flashback,Younger Souma,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.20,0:12:37.30,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Look...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.54,0:12:42.75,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Wanting to do something \Nfor others is a good thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.00,0:12:46.61,Flashback,Younger Souma,0,0,0,,I feel like you'd be a good teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.61,0:12:47.54,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.54,0:12:52.52,Flashback,Younger Souma,0,0,0,,You'd be one of those teachers that \Nprotects every student, like a hero!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.52,0:12:53.47,Flashback,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,You think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.47,0:12:54.54,Flashback,Younger Souma,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.07,0:12:58.46,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,He left without even telling me his name.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.45,0:13:05.45,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,A few years later, we met again \Nat the Ca—I mean, at a facility.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.53,0:13:09.17,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Fate had changed him by then.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.59,0:13:14.16,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,He may be a hero in my eyes, \Nbut he's still human.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.48,0:13:17.79,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I couldn't blame him for wanting to survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.79,0:13:19.49,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Whether it was murder or destruction,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.49,0:13:23.99,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I told myself it was to repay him \Nfor saving my life. But...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.37,0:13:28.71,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I wonder if this is really...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.84,0:13:35.01,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Who knew Shinozaki Sensei had \Nsuch a passionate side to him?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.01,0:13:37.17,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Wha—When did you figure that out?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.17,0:13:38.67,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,From the beginning, of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.67,0:13:43.61,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,It was obvious you were just pretending to \Nrun into me to gauge if Sensei was with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.61,0:13:44.85,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Why you—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.85,0:13:47.33,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,You should give him \Na good smack on the face.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.33,0:13:48.38,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.27,0:13:53.10,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,If he goes back to the hero you loved, great.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.75,0:13:58.44,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,If not, do as you please. \NCook him for all I care.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.98,0:14:04.36,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Cook? Man, you sure are a weird one.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.36,0:14:08.87,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Weird and complex, just how humans \Nshould be. You should remember that!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.41,0:14:13.42,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Do me a favor. \NCan you take me to your group?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.42,0:14:14.33,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.33,0:14:17.58,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Shinozaki-san will likely use \Nhis Prime Right to come find me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.58,0:14:20.48,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I want to settle things in front of you guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.48,0:14:25.19,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Just one condition. Tell me \Nabout your Materialization Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.19,0:14:26.50,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Sure, no problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.50,0:14:28.51,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Oh, well that was easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.98,0:14:30.58,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,My Materialization Right is a Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.58,0:14:32.67,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,that brings drawings \Nand pictures to real life.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.67,0:14:35.73,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Creatures are under my full command,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.73,0:14:38.98,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,which is why I carry card games \Non me as my primary weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.60,0:14:42.32,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,But it's exhausting, since\Nit's under the Protection Attribute.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.32,0:14:44.45,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Not to mention, I've sacrificed my right lung.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.45,0:14:46.87,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,So I can only use my powers \Nthree or four times a day.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.87,0:14:49.20,Italics,Eren,0,0,0,,He sure talks a lot...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.45,0:14:52.33,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,You know, I can tell that you're pretty dumb.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.33,0:14:55.04,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,You could tell?! Just how much \Ndo you already know?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.04,0:14:56.21,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Yikes...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.76,0:14:59.16,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Oh, well. I have something \Nto show you guys anyways.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.16,0:15:00.71,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Better hurry and find them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.71,0:15:02.06,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,But isn't it dangerous?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.06,0:15:04.42,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Don't worry, you'll be with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.14,0:15:08.80,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,You're Shinozaki-san's precious student. \NI won't let anything happen to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.11,0:15:12.86,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,You really believe you'll meet \Nyour hero again, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.94,0:15:16.48,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,You're that guy from—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.88,0:15:18.82,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,You must be Saneatsu Narita!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.82,0:15:21.69,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I'm Hayato Souma. Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.69,0:15:24.24,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Eren Senpai, get away from him!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.24,0:15:25.98,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Wait, hang on!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.98,0:15:28.38,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Simmer down. I just wanna talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.63,0:15:32.60,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,A red laptop?! Fine...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.60,0:15:36.71,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Well, if there's no way you'll trust me, \NI can just hand over this—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.71,0:15:37.71,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.17,0:15:39.64,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Don't do anything else!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.46,0:15:43.72,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,There's a possibility that a man \Nnamed Mido will steal your laptop
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.72,0:15:47.49,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,the moment you abandon ownership of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.49,0:15:49.50,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,We sure don't want that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.50,0:15:52.47,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Regardless, coming into possession \Nof a laptop is the hardest part.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.03,0:15:55.81,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Lucky for us, you've found one already.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.99,0:15:58.85,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Here, take the adapter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.85,0:16:02.98,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,There's no remaining battery, so \Nthere's no using the laptop without this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.98,0:16:04.03,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,You can be sure it's safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.52,0:16:07.93,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I've entered the password so we're fine \Nuntil the end of the day tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.93,0:16:09.61,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Haven't submitted any questions, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.61,0:16:11.53,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,That should make it safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.53,0:16:13.82,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,With Souma as the current owner, \Nwe have no choice
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.82,0:16:17.21,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,but to stick with him \Nto protect the laptop—
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.49,0:16:19.37,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.48,0:16:22.94,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Shinozaki-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.94,0:16:26.09,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Souma... Why are you with Narita?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.01,0:16:31.24,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,No! It's not what you think!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.24,0:16:32.35,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Shinozaki-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.95,0:16:37.27,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I've decided to work with them \Nto defeat the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.86,0:16:39.17,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,What about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.86,0:16:43.23,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Souma...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.68,0:16:45.57,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Let's settle this,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.57,0:16:48.28,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,in front of the students you betrayed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.24,0:16:55.57,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.41,0:17:01.14,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I won't ask for forgiveness. \NI don't expect you to forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.14,0:17:03.00,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It was all entirely my wrongdoing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.78,0:17:05.31,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Shinozaki-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.31,0:17:07.19,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,We can't accept that after all you've—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.19,0:17:11.37,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Of course not! But please, \Nbelieve what I'm about to tell you!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.19,0:17:14.60,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Sudo is dead!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.34,0:17:17.83,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Sudo Senpai?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.83,0:17:18.75,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,That can't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.15,0:17:24.11,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Do you have any proof? \NAny messages or belongings he left you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.41,0:17:27.56,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I have documents and notes he \Nentrusted me with. Other than that...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.94,0:17:31.24,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I remember him using \Na special type of fire powder.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.24,0:17:34.61,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Something about magicians \Nand his friend lending it to him...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.22,0:17:39.22,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,That's more than enough. \NI believe Sensei is telling the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.22,0:17:40.08,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,President?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.08,0:17:41.96,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,The rest of you don't need to believe him.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.73,0:17:45.24,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,But trust me when I say he's being truthful.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.29,0:17:48.18,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,I trust him, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.61,0:17:51.55,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,All right. So?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.12,0:17:55.76,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,According to Sudo's notes, the Emperor's \NPrime Right is the Recovery Right,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.76,0:17:57.97,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,and their objective is \Nto recover other Prime Rights.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.97,0:18:00.14,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Senpai had the same theory...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.14,0:18:04.35,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,So why did Tasuketsu begin \Nin Suginami of all places?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.35,0:18:07.07,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,That's because "Saneatsu Narita \Nwas in Suginami".
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.07,0:18:08.12,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.12,0:18:08.94,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.94,0:18:10.32,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,What does {\i1}that{\i0} mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.32,0:18:12.47,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Sudo went on to say this:
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.92,0:18:16.41,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Saneatsu Narita should already \Npossess some kind of Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.41,0:18:18.93,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,That thought crossed my mind, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.93,0:18:21.87,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,That would explain why \NI couldn't open the envelope...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.25,0:18:24.02,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It all began with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.02,0:18:25.58,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,A newspaper clipping?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.92,0:18:29.57,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,An article about my accident \Nfrom when I was four...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.77,0:18:31.80,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.80,0:18:36.05,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(320,20)\bord4}"...caused by the father's friend"
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.20,0:18:34.44,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,It was caused by my dad's friend?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.44,0:18:35.70,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,You never knew?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.30,0:18:38.40,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Sudo's theory was this:
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.40,0:18:42.64,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Narita's father hired his friend \Nto cause the accident and harm you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.64,0:18:44.52,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,But why would my dad do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.89,0:18:46.86,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,These are your medical records \Nfrom the accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.15,0:18:46.86,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0}Saneatsu Narita's Medical Records
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.86,0:18:49.27,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It says right here...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.27,0:18:53.03,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,"Saneatsu Narita: Loss of one kidney due to \Ninjuries sustained in the accident."
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.27,0:18:53.03,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(320,20)\bord4}Loss of one kidney due to injuries sustained in the accident
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.03,0:18:56.13,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,"Loss"? You mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.13,0:18:59.93,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Most likely, he used your surgery as \Na means to forcefully sacrifice your kidney
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.93,0:19:02.88,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,in return for a Prime Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.88,0:19:04.49,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,How could that be possible?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.49,0:19:07.20,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I never even told Sudo Senpai \Nabout my accident!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.20,0:19:10.17,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Sudo first took notice of Jin and myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.17,0:19:13.64,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Oh, is that cuz I already had a Prime Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.64,0:19:14.63,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.76,0:19:16.89,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(320,80)\bord0\b1\fs40\fad(1,1600)}Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.26,0:19:20.48,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Prime Rights directly relate to Tasuketsu, \Nand Tasuketsu directly relates to the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.05,0:19:18.26,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(320,80)\bord0\b1\fs40\fad(250,400)}Tasuketsu
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.18,0:19:20.05,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord0\b1\fs15\fad(650,400)\pos(339,67)}Emperor
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.26,0:19:20.05,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord0\b1\fs15\fad(650,400)\pos(210,114)}Tasuketsu
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.91,0:19:25.73,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Assuming the Emperor intentionally \Nbegan Tasuketsu in Suginami...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.72,0:19:25.73,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord0\b1\fad(680,1)\pos(326,149)}Suginami Ward
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.02,0:19:28.56,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,...led Sudo to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.23,0:19:26.35,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs25\frz1\pos(330,38)\3c&HFFFFFF&\c&H944A2C&\bord2\3a&H79&}Gunjosora Orphanage
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.35,0:19:26.48,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs25\frz1\pos(330,131)\3c&HFFFFFF&\c&H944A2C&\bord2\3a&H79&}Gunjosora Orphanage
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.48,0:19:26.60,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(330,57)\frz1\3c&HFFFFFF&\3a&H5D&}Children's Home
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.48,0:19:26.60,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs25\frz1\pos(330,208)\3c&HFFFFFF&\c&H944A2C&\bord2\3a&H79&}Gunjosora Orphanage
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.60,0:19:26.73,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(330,108)\frz1\3c&HFFFFFF&\3a&H5D&}Children's Home
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.60,0:19:26.73,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs25\frz1\pos(330,260)\3c&HFFFFFF&\c&H944A2C&\bord2\3a&H79&}Gunjosora Orphanage
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.73,0:19:28.56,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(330,124)\frz1\3c&HFFFFFF&\3a&H5D&}Children's Home
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.73,0:19:28.56,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs25\frz1\pos(330,276)\3c&HFFFFFF&\c&H944A2C&\bord2\3a&H79&}Gunjosora Orphanage
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.56,0:19:30.31,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Gunjosora Orphanage!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.31,0:19:32.76,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Wait, pea size. You know this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.76,0:19:37.16,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,After I escaped the Camp, \Nthey took care of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.16,0:19:40.01,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,For real?! They took me in, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.01,0:19:41.03,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Me, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.20,0:19:44.83,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,The Director is named Yugo Shimahara.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.95,0:19:47.79,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\pos(320,235)}Suspect Yugo Shimahara
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.77,0:19:47.47,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,He's the man who hit Narita.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.52,0:19:51.58,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,A friend of Dad's... An orphanage...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.25,0:19:54.45,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,A kidney in return for a Prime Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.70,0:19:59.51,Flashback,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Is your dad still living overseas?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.64,0:20:02.64,Flashback,Omi,0,0,0,,It used to have branches overseas, too...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.76,0:20:06.27,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\shad0\bord0\pos(323,348)}Prime Right Access Denied
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.20,0:20:06.27,Flashback - Top,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,I can't acquire a Prime Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.74,0:20:09.95,Default,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,The more I think about it, \Nthe more it makes sense...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.28,0:20:12.64,Default,Saaya,0,0,0,,Saneatsu...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.44,0:20:16.19,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,And the note also states this:
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.32,0:20:18.15,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0\frz-1\pos(277,18)\b0}Narita Saneatsu\N\Nis the key
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.15,0:20:22.08,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,The Prime Right entrusted to Narita \Nshould be the key to defeating the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.95,0:20:26.57,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,So Narita-kun's father was taking up \Narms against the organization
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.57,0:20:28.89,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,while being a member himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.89,0:20:29.79,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Precisely.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.12,0:20:33.12,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,He knew that the birth of a \Nsuccessful subject was imminent,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.12,0:20:35.41,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,so he passed down the only \Nhope he had to his own son.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.41,0:20:37.71,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,But I thought you couldn't \Nknow what Prime Rights are
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.71,0:20:39.65,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,in each envelope for real until you open it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.65,0:20:41.90,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,How did he choose Saneatsu's Prime Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.90,0:20:46.07,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Sudo suspected there was another collaborator \Nwith a Prime Right that made it possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.07,0:20:49.05,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Perhaps a researcher who \Nprovided help in a limited scope
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.05,0:20:51.38,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,under certain conditions and circumstances.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.38,0:20:54.90,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,That's a crazy-detailed theory, for real...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.16,0:20:56.74,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,That's the overall picture.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.08,0:21:01.99,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,The details are still unclear. There's just \Ntoo many elements intertwined in the story.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.55,0:21:05.40,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Either way, we have our hope right here!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.20,0:21:08.54,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Saneatsu Narita is the key to everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.75,0:21:12.33,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Engage Transillumination Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.87,0:21:12.67,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,600)\bord0\pos(322,267)}Right
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.67,0:21:14.50,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,1)\bord0\pos(322,267)\c&H2B2D28&\1a&H85&}Portrait\NRight
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.20,0:21:16.92,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Aww, man. Another fail.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.92,0:21:19.92,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,Assemble
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.72,0:21:19.25,Default,Mido,0,0,0,,Too bad.
